#lang fhir/sd

;;; Profiles authored in the StructureDefinition language. Each `profile` constrains a base type; the
;;; constraints are checked at COMPILE time and the profile compiles to a delegating form macro. A
;;; profile may base on another profile, giving multi-level delegation (VIP → USCorePatient →
;;; Patient → typed node). Loosening a cardinality is a compile error.

;; A US-Core-style Patient: name and gender are required.
(profile USCorePatient #:base Patient
  (name   1 *)
  (gender 1 1))

;; A profile OF a profile: a VIP must have exactly one name (narrowing USCorePatient's 1..*).
(profile VIPPatient #:base USCorePatient
  (name 1 1))
